7... g5
{ It's important not to be afraid to play g5. We haven't castled yet, so we're not afraid to push the pawns in front of our king. If the king were on g8, you'd have to watch out for a knight sacrifice, but here it's not dangerous. }
8. Bg3 { White retreats to g3. } 8... Bg4
{ Now we bring our bishop out to g4. The difference is that now if white tries h3, the g-pawn is blocked by white's own bishop on g3. The bishop has no prospects - it's trapped by pawns with no squares to go to. }
9. h3
{ If white plays h3 trying to chase the bishop, their g-pawn is blocked by their own bishop on g3. }
9... Bh5
{ We move the bishop back to h5. The bishop on g3 is trapped with no way out. }
